{"entities":"[{\"text\": \"piperazine\", \"id\": \"C034930\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"trans-2-amino-3-hydroxy-1, 2, 3, 4-tetrahydroanaphthalene\", \"id\": \"-1\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"N-(trans-3-hydroxy-1,2,3,4-tetrahydro-2-naphthyl)-N-(3-oxo-3-phenyl-2-methylpropyl)-piperazine hydrochloride\", \"id\": \"C013741\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"P11\", \"id\": \"C013741\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"arrhythmia\", \"id\": \"D001145\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"BaCl2\", \"id\": \"C024986\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"chloroform\", \"id\": \"D002725\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"adrenaline\", \"id\": \"D004837\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"strophantine G\", \"id\": \"D010042\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"aconitine\", \"id\": \"D000157\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"P11\", \"id\": \"C013741\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"arrhythmia\", \"id\": \"D001145\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"arrhythmia\", \"id\": \"D001145\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"chloroform\", \"id\": \"D002725\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"adrenaline\", \"id\": \"D004837\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"BaCl2\", \"id\": \"C024986\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}]","filtered_entities":[{"text":"trans-2-amino-3-hydroxy-1, 2, 3, 4-tetrahydroanaphthalene","id":"-1","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"N-(trans-3-hydroxy-1,2,3,4-tetrahydro-2-naphthyl)-N-(3-oxo-3-phenyl-2-methylpropyl)-piperazine hydrochloride","id":"C013741","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"P11","id":"C013741","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"arrhythmia","id":"D001145","label":"Disease"},{"text":"BaCl2","id":"C024986","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"chloroform","id":"D002725","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"adrenaline","id":"D004837","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"strophantine G","id":"D010042","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"aconitine","id":"D000157","label":"Chemical"}],"head":"aconitine","head_id":"D000157","pairs":[{"head":"trans-2-amino-3-hydroxy-1, 2, 3, 4-tetrahydroanaphthalene","tail":"arrhythmia","head_id":"-1","tail_id":"D001145"},{"head":"N-(trans-3-hydroxy-1,2,3,4-tetrahydro-2-naphthyl)-N-(3-oxo-3-phenyl-2-methylpropyl)-piperazine hydrochloride","tail":"arrhythmia","head_id":"C013741","tail_id":"D001145"},{"head":"BaCl2","tail":"arrhythmia","head_id":"C024986","tail_id":"D001145"},{"head":"chloroform","tail":"arrhythmia","head_id":"D002725","tail_id":"D001145"},{"head":"adrenaline","tail":"arrhythmia","head_id":"D004837","tail_id":"D001145"},{"head":"strophantine G","tail":"arrhythmia","head_id":"D010042","tail_id":"D001145"},{"head":"aconitine","tail":"arrhythmia","head_id":"D000157","tail_id":"D001145"}],"relations":["C024986 | D001145","D002725 | D001145","D004837 | D001145","D010042 | D001145","D000157 | D001145"],"result":"$","tail":"arrhythmia","tail_id":"D001145","text":"On the antiarrhythmic activity of one N-substituted piperazine derivative of trans-2-amino-3-hydroxy-1, 2, 3, 4-tetrahydroanaphthalene. The antiarrhythmic activity of the compound N-(trans-3-hydroxy-1,2,3,4-tetrahydro-2-naphthyl)-N-(3-oxo-3-phenyl-2-methylpropyl)-piperazine hydrochloride, referred to as P11, is studied on anaesthesized cats and Wistar albino rats, as well as on non-anaesthesized rabbits. Four types of experimental arrhythmia are used--with BaCl2, with chloroform-adrenaline, with strophantine G and with aconitine. The compound P11 is introduced in doses of 0.25 and 0.50 mg/kg intravenously and 10 mg/kg orally. The compound manifests antiarrhythmic activity in all models of experimental arrhythmia used, causing greatest inhibition on the arrhythmia induced by chloroform-adrenaline (in 90 per cent) and with BaCl2 (in 84 per cent). The results obtained are associated with the beta-adrenoblocking and with the membrane-stabilizing action of the compound.","metrics":{"precision":1.0,"recall":1.0,"f1":1.0,"rel_tp":5,"rel_fp":0,"rel_fn":0}}